WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.777 --> 00:00:22.383
The graph places you in the centre. Every dot is a person, coloured by their primary circle, and sized by relationship strength.

2
00:00:22.383 --> 00:00:29.285
Lines are relationships. Solid lines come from your sources and email threads; dashed lines connect people at the same company.

3
00:00:29.285 --> 00:00:37.799
Rings around a dot show that the person is in more than one circle.

4
00:00:37.799 --> 00:00:47.067
Use the lens chips to focus on one circle. Here is just the Corporate circle: your colleagues.

5
00:00:47.067 --> 00:00:56.236
And the Business circle.

6
00:00:56.236 --> 00:01:03.906
Search filters the graph by name, company or email as you type.

7
00:01:03.906 --> 00:01:13.494
The strength slider hides weaker relationships so the people who matter most stand out.

8
00:01:13.494 --> 00:01:21.108
Cluster by circle pulls each circle into its own region of the canvas.

9
00:01:21.108 --> 00:01:25.778
Cluster by company groups colleagues together.

10
00:01:25.778 --> 00:01:34.861
Scroll to zoom, drag the background to pan, and drag a person to pin them while the layout settles.

11
00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:40.858
Hover for a quick summary. Click a person to open their side sheet.

12
00:01:40.858 --> 00:01:49.450
The sheet shows strength, interactions, sources and the people they are connected to. Open takes you to the full profile.

13
00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:53.936
The toolbar zooms, fits the graph to the window and re-runs the layout.
